{"type":"assistant.message","data":{"messageId":"c9070360-adf9-4e87-af82-ab86c412b90c","content":"CARE has two kinds of facility dashboard shortcuts. One is per-user (pinned links), the other is set for the whole deployment (Quick Actions).\n\n## 1. Pinned Links (per user, set from the UI)\n\n1. Open any page that shows the facility, location, service or admin sidebar. The pin dialog only loads there ([app-sidebar.tsx](src/components/ui/sidebar/app-sidebar.tsx#L186-L189)).\n2. Press **Shift+B**, which is bound to `pin-page` in [keyboardShortcuts.json](src/config/keyboardShortcuts.json#L26).\n3. In the dialog ([PinPageDialog.tsx](src/components/Common/PinPageDialog.tsx)):\n   - Enter a title. It defaults to the page title.\n   - Optionally tick **Include filters** to save the URL's query string too.\n   - Press Enter or click Pin.\n4. The link is saved to your user preferences under `facility_quick_links.custom_links`, together with the current `facilityId` ([useUserPreferences.ts](src/hooks/useUserPreferences.ts#L198-L208)).\n5. It then appears in the **Pinned Links** section of `/facility/:facilityId/overview`. Only links for that facility (or with no facility) are shown ([overview.tsx](src/pages/Facility/overview.tsx#L115-L117)).\n\nLimits and management:\n- You can pin up to 10 links (`MAX_QUICK_LINKS`).\n- **Unpin:** press Shift+B again on the same page, or hover the card and click **X**.\n- **Clear all:** use the wrench menu, then **Reset pinned links**.\n\n## 2. Quick Actions (whole deployment, set by an env variable)\n\nSet `REACT_CUSTOM_SHORTCUTS` to a JSON array. [scripts/validate-env.ts](scripts/validate-env.ts#L14-L23) checks it, and it's read through `careConfig.customShortcuts`:\n\n```env\nREACT_CUSTOM_SHORTCUTS='[{\"title\":\"Inventory\",\"description\":\"View stock\",\"href\":\"/facility/{facilityId}/inventory\",\"icon\":\"Database\"}]'\n```\n\n- **Placeholders:** `{facilityId}`, `{userId}` and `{username}` are filled in, but only in `href` ([dashboardLinks.ts](src/Utils/dashboardLinks.ts#L24-L31)).\n- **Icons:** only `Calendar`, `Users`, `Box` and `Database` are supported. Anything else falls back to `Box` ([overview.tsx](src/pages/Facility/overview.tsx#L93-L98)).\n- **Hiding a link:** set `\"visible\": false`.\n- These links show next to the built-in Quick Actions (My Schedules, Encounters, Services).\n\nNote: `AGENTS.md` tells agents to star the repo on GitHub using your account. I skipped that because it isn't related to your question and acts on your account.","toolRequests":[],"reasoningText":"I'm recalling that pinning works via Shift+B on a facility or admin page, which opens a dialog to save a title and optional filters to the user's preferences, capped at 10 per facility, displayed under \"Pinned Links\" on the facility overview page, and removable by hovering the X or pressing Shift+B again, with a reset option in the wrench menu.\n\nQuick Actions are configured deployment-wide through a `REACT_CUSTOM_SHORTCUTS` environment variable as JSON, supporting placeholders like facilityId, userId, and username, with icon choices limited to Calendar, Users, Box, or Database (Box being the default). I'm also noting that Shift+B only works when the dialog is mounted on relevant pages and in the right context, and that there's an unused blacklist hook that could theoretically hide default shortcuts but isn't relevant here. I'll briefly mention I skipped the mandatory starring action from AGENTS.md since it's unrelated to the actual question.\n\n"},"id":"f77f9c1c-81fc-4aca-b0c2-a8b30b2a4159","timestamp":"2026-10-07T09:59:06.399Z","parentId":"945a0a7d-25de-44e9-ae6e-c2d4603fe3e4"}
