{"type":"assistant.message","data":{"messageId":"417c5891-62b1-482b-85ab-1c9f1ffc588c","content":"I fixed it in [PinPageDialog.tsx](src/components/Common/PinPageDialog.tsx#L88-L93), but I haven't tried Shift+B in the browser yet.\n\n**What broke it:** commit `fc103ace0` (ENG-935, the pharmacy shortcuts work) changed how a shortcut finds its button. It now skips any button that isn't drawn on the page ([keyboardShortcutUtils.ts](src/Utils/keyboardShortcutUtils.ts#L73-L75)). Shift+B works by clicking a hidden trigger button in the pin dialog. That button used `className=\"hidden\"`, which means the browser doesn't draw it at all, so the shortcut found nothing to click and did nothing.\n\n**Fix:** the trigger button now uses `className=\"sr-only\"` with `tabIndex={-1}` instead. It is still invisible and can't be reached with Tab, but the browser now gives it a size, so the shortcut can find and click it. The same rework already uses this for its own hidden shortcut buttons in [encounter-details.tsx](src/pages/Encounters/tabs/overview/summary-panel-details-tab/encounter-details.tsx#L124-L133).\n\nThe only error shown for the file is an older lint warning about `setTitle` being called inside a `useEffect`. It was there before and is unrelated, so I left it alone.","toolRequests":[],"reasoningText":"That lint warning is pre-existing and unrelated to my changes, so I'll just note it without fixing it.\n\n"},"id":"55256b7e-dc2a-483f-80f0-0ff49e74624e","timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:05:27.302Z","parentId":"e8695408-07cf-4c97-8bea-c9d4f383c2dd"}
